\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


For $n\geq1$, let $S^{n+1}(1)=\{x\in\mathbb R^{n+2}:\lVert x\rVert=1\}$ with its standard round metric. Let $M^n\subset S^{n+1}(1)$ be a connected smooth closed embedded hypersurface, with the induced metric, whose mean-curvature vector is identically zero. Let $\Delta_M=\operatorname{div}_M\nabla_M$; $\lambda_1(M)$ denotes the least positive eigenvalue of the nonnegative operator $-\Delta_M$, equivalently
\[
\lambda_1(M)=\inf_{\substack{f\in C^\infty(M,\mathbb R),\ f\not\equiv0\\\int_M f\,dV=0}}
\frac{\int_M\lVert\nabla_Mf\rVert^2\,dV}{\int_M f^2\,dV}.
\]
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is $\lambda_1(M)=n$ for every connected closed embedded minimal hypersurface $M^n\subset S^{n+1}(1)$? \href{https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.06123}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does every closed embedded minimal hypersurface of the unit sphere have first nonzero Laplace eigenvalue equal to its dimension?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{description}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 1212 (GEO-021). CC BY 4.0. \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Lingzhong Zeng, \emph{The First Eigenvalue of Embedded Minimal Hypersurfaces in the Unit Sphere I: Yau\textquotesingle s Conjecture}, arXiv:2508.06123v1 (2025), Section 1, displayed Yau conjecture. \url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.06123}.
\end{description}
